+## CR4 batch A7: masks, neckwear, backpieces, gloves, wristwear, belts, ear jewellery, piercings (2026-11-15)
+
+The accessory rows of CREATOR_PLAN 3.1 are deep fields saved in the CR5 look pool. First tranche: **111 new parts live**.
+
+| slot (catalog key) | deep field | live | planned | file |
+|---|---|--:|--:|---|
+| Masks (`mask`) | `DF_MASK` | 17 | 36 | `core/data/parts/acc/mask.txt` |
+| Neckwear (`neck`) | `DF_NECK` | 20 | 52 | `acc/neck.txt` |
+| Backpieces (`back`) | `DF_BACK` | 19 | 52 | `acc/back.txt` |
+| Gloves (`gloves`) | `DF_GLOVE` | 9 | 18 | `acc/gloves.txt` |
+| Wristwear (`wrist`) | `DF_WRIST` | 9 | 18 | `acc/wrist.txt` |
+| Belts (`belt`) | `DF_BELT` | 13 | 24 | `acc/belt.txt` |
+| Ear jewellery (`ear_acc`) | `DF_EARJEW` | 14 | 28 | `acc/ear_acc.txt` |
+| Face piercings (`face_pierce`) | `DF_PIERCE` | 10 | 16 | `acc/face_pierce.txt` |
+
+**Left for A7b:** 133 parts (masks 19, neckwear 32, backpieces 33, gloves and wristwear 18, belts 11, ear jewellery 14, piercings 6).
+
+* **Deep field ids.** The eight new fields sit in the pool range right after `DF_LINER` (`look_fields.h`); the painted-only fields
+  (bags, freckles, moles, scars, make-up, face paint, aura 2) moved behind them, out of the range, so the creator's per-undo-step
+  arrays grow by 8 bytes a snapshot only for the new fields and not for those seven. `DF_LASH`, `DF_LID` and `DF_LINER` (6, 7, 8) did not move:
+  saves from CR5 load as before. (`parts_build.py` and `partcat_build.py` now skip comments when they read the enum.)
+* **Painters.** `PS_DEEP` / `PS_DEEP_FRAME` (`portrait_int.h`): masks, piercings and ear jewellery in `ph_face_acc` (group 5), neckwear in
+  `neck_acc` (group 4), backpieces in `back_acc` (group 0, before wings and tail), belts after the top and outer layer (group 1), gloves
+  and wristwear in a frame at each hand (`hand_acc`: gloves 128 = the paw radius, wristwear a fifth up the arm). None is chibi-visible.
+* **Creator.** Outfit tab "Dress-ups" (Mask, Neckwear, Backpiece, Gloves, Wristwear, Belt, Ear jewellery) and Face tab "Face jewellery" (Piercings)
+  through `RK_DEEP` rows; their colour is the Acc. colour. Piercings are age class teen (never on a child); everything else all ages.
+* **Pool cost.** A deep choice costs 2 bytes in a citizen's pool run, at most 22 bytes for all eleven fields.
+* **Sheets.** `portrait_sheet --slot KEY` (`--views` for the body slots), `--interplay-acc` (`interplay_back_N`: backpieces x wings, cape,
+  tail, from behind; `interplay_mask_N`: masks x horns, glasses, top hat, big hair, hood).
+* **Tests.** `test_cr4_a7.c`: ids, lists, scripted, ages, cost cap, every part draws, every pair differs by the slot's gate summed over bust,
+  figure and the fighter front and back (gates are measured and small for tiny parts such as piercings), chibi unchanged, pool run resolves.
+* **PS1.** No part VM yet (CR10): the PS1 creator does not offer these rows (`LOOK_POOL_SAVED` 0). GBA / Dreamcast offer them.
